  "note": [
    {
      "text": "Confirmed at the dental visit: the plaque-induced gingivitis (K05.00) found at the well-child visit has progressed. Coded as aggressive periodontitis, localized, slight (ICD-10-CM K05.211, verified against the 2026 ICD-10-CM). 'Aggressive' rather than 'chronic' is deliberate and clinically correct: chronic periodontitis is a slow adult disease, whereas the rapid breakdown in a six-year-old with poorly controlled Type 1 diabetes (E10.9) is the aggressive pattern. This Condition is linked to the diabetes as a contributing systemic condition and is transmitted in the Interaction 4 bidirectional summaries."
    }
